>Well I think it'd be a laugh.

Hmm.  Considering how much trash you pick up from monsters in this game
and dump just to lighten your pack

      (I'm doing a "base sticker" act on a neutral altar on level
      four just now, trying to push my experience level up past my
      current level 16, I've been at this altar for over 50,000
      moves, and I have carried so much trash to the next level up
      to get it out of the way, the floor is starting to sag. I've
      nailed four named weapons and an AC of -14 so far; I just
      want to see if the game ever really forces you to go find
      the wizard. I'm doing it the hard way, too, as the Hand of
      Elbereth, so it is a lot longer between prayers than between
      meals.  My stack of armor alone, cursed stuff excluded, takes
      four screens to display.),

it would be an added giggle if you developed your picture several levels
after you dumped some worthless looking fourth seemingly identical sword
and an excess pair of gloves *somewhere* behind you, to find out:

: Dead orc, carrying Frostbrand and wearing blessed +4 gloves of dexterity :

I've always felt, compared to Rogue, Hack and Nethack make it _much_ too
difficult to identify things.  Could this be an added, tremendously
inconvenient (you can only photograph something a monster is carrying)
way to identify a little more stuff?

